  "notes": [
    "[THIS PRODUCT] Features a flavor profile highlighted by captivating earthy and spicy notes with subtle sweet undertones.",
    "[GENERAL] Sumatran coffees are traditionally processed using wet-hulling (locally known as *Giling Basah*), an Indonesian method that imparts low acidity, dense body, and deep, rustic complexity.",
    "[GENERAL] Dark-roasted Sumatran beans are ideally suited for full-immersion methods like a French press or cold brew, where metal filtration leaves the coffee's rich natural oils in the cup rather than absorbing them into paper.",
    "[GENERAL] For French press brewing, use a coarse grind with water heated to 195°F–205°F, steep for 4 minutes at a standard 1:15 to 1:16 coffee-to-water ratio, and press gently to avoid extracting harsh bitterness."
